(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The limited C API's next slices (queue 262; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 262\"; the user's 244-3 (a) and"] [4 1 "// 244-4 (a)): the functions CPython 3.14.10's Modules/_testlimitedcapi (built by ci into the world beside"] [5 1 "// _ctypes_test) and the pythonapi tests reach, as natives over the handles, ported from CPython 3.14.10's"] [6 1 "// Objects/ (capsule.c, sliceobject.c, moduleobject.c, abstract.c, object.c, longobject.c), Python/ (getargs.c,"] [7 1 "// modsupport.c, ceval.c, sysmodule.c, errors.c, pystrcmp.c, getversion.c) and Include/ (the limited API's"] [8 1 "// declarations, the constants). The PSF's license (LICENSE.md)."] [9 1 "//"] [10 1 "// A function the world's C calls and pyi does not provide is a native that raises NotImplementedError \"pyi's C API"] [11 1 "// does not provide NAME\" (capiMissing: the C stack unwound to the Python call that entered C, as a longjmp would),"] [12 1 "// so a module of the world loads whole and each of its functions fails alone, by a message the classes match."] [25 1 "// capiMissing is the panic of a C API function pyi does not provide."] [28 1 "// missingNative is the native of an undefined C API function."] [33 1 "// recoverMissing turns a capiMissing panic into the Python exception *err (the C stack is restored by World.guard)."] [45 1 "// isCAPIName is a name of the C API (its functions' prefixes)."] [50 1 "// bindMissing makes every undefined C API function of the world a missingNative."] [63 1 "// ---- the C API's data: types and exceptions ----"] [65 1 "// capiTypes are the type objects the limited API names as data (Include/*object.h's PyAPI_DATA(PyTypeObject))."] [76 1 "// bindTypes binds the type objects' structs first (queue 269: every handle made after names them, as ob_type and"] [77 1 "// tp_base), then fills each as CPython's PyTypeObject."] [92 2 "// the types the full API's macros name that pyi's runtime has under another module's name (PyFunction_Check,"] [93 2 "// PyWeakref_CheckRef ...): bound by the type the module gives"] [126 1 "// capsuleType is PyCapsule's type (py's)."] [129 1 "// bindData binds the world's C API data: the type objects' structs become the types' handles, each PyExc_NAME"] [130 1 "// pointer the handle of builtins.NAME, _Py_EllipsisObject and _Py_NotImplementedStruct their singletons'."] [155 1 "// The offsets of _PyRuntime.static_objects.singletons.strings' one-character strings, as ci lays out CPython 3.14.10's"] [156 1 "// _PyRuntimeState (Include/internal/pycore_runtime_structs.h, pycore_global_strings.h) on 64 bits: the node program's"] [157 1 "// _Py_LATIN1_CHR reads them (_testclinic's deprecation checks: PySequence_Contains(kwnames, _Py_LATIN1_CHR('c'))) and"] [158 1 "// _PyLong_GetZero's static_objects offset."] [160 48 "// offsetof(_PyRuntimeState, static_objects)"] [161 48 "// .singletons (first), then .strings in it"] [162 48 "// .ascii[128]: struct { PyASCIIObject _ascii; uint8_t _data[2]; }"] [163 48 "// .latin1[128]: struct { PyCompactUnicodeObject _latin1; uint8_t _data[2]; }"] [166 27 "// sizeof(_PyRuntimeState): the static's size the offsets are checked against"] [169 1 "// bindStaticStrings binds _PyRuntime's static one-character strings (queue 475, 473-3 (a); Include/internal/"] [170 1 "// pycore_unicodeobject.h's _Py_LATIN1_CHR, a C module built with Py_BUILD_CORE): each of the 256 slots becomes the"] [171 1 "// handle of a str of its character, immortal, with its compact layout written in place (CPython's"] [172 1 "// _PyASCIIObject_INIT and _PyUnicode_LATIN1_INIT: ASCII ones a PyASCIIObject, the others a PyCompactUnicodeObject),"] [173 1 "// so C reads a real object there. Nothing when the world has no _PyRuntime or it is not the size these offsets are of."] [174 1 "// (_Py_ID's identifiers and _Py_STR's literals before the arrays: no C of the world names one.)"] [197 1 "// ---- helpers ----"] [199 1 "// excOf is the exception object the error indicator holds (nil: none)."] [207 1 "// badInternalCall is PyErr_BadInternalCall's SystemError."] [210 1 "// errInt sets the error indicator and gives the int -1."] [216 1 "// result is a new reference to o, or C's NULL with err set."] [224 1 "// cstrOrNil is a C string argument (nil for NULL)."] [232 1 "// fromUTF8 is PyUnicode_FromString's decoding of a C string."] [241 1 "// keepCString is s as a C string that lives as long as the process (a const char * the C API returns as borrowed"] [242 1 "// from an object CPython would hold: tp_name, ml_name, a version string), made once per distinct string."] [254 1 "// ssize is a Py_ssize_t clamp of an int (PyLong_AsSsize_t's overflow aside)."] [267 1 "// asLong is PyLong_AsLong (Objects/longobject.c): an int, or an object with __index__."] [283 1 "// asUnsignedMask is PyLong_AsUnsignedLongMask: the int's low 64 bits."] [293 1 "// ---- modules (Objects/moduleobject.c, Python/modsupport.c) ----"] [295 1 "// moduleOf is the module (or its dict) a module handle names."] [303 1 "// addFunctions is PyModule_AddFunctions: each PyMethodDef of the table at defs a built-in function of the module,"] [304 1 "// its self the module."] [332 1 "// cMethod is a PyCFunction of the world bound to self (PyCFunction_NewEx's object)."] [340 2 "// a type's method (queue 268): self is the call's first argument (selfFirst, but METH_STATIC's), defining its"] [341 2 "// type (METH_METHOD's defining_class), qual its name in the messages (Type.name)"] [351 1 "// Builtin is the method as pyi's built-in function."] [356 1 "// call is the vectorcall of a PyCFunction (Objects/methodobject.c: cfunction_call and the METH_* trampolines)."] [360 2 "// the messages name the function as _PyObject_FunctionStr does: module.name() (Objects/methodobject.c)"] [382 25 "// METH_METHOD | METH_FASTCALL | METH_KEYWORDS: (self, defining_class, args, nargsf, kwnames)"] [403 24 "// METH_FASTCALL (| METH_KEYWORDS)"] [425 23 "// METH_NOARGS"] [431 23 "// METH_O"] [437 11 "// METH_VARARGS (| METH_KEYWORDS)"] [477 1 "// moduleFromDef is PyModule_Create2's module: m_name, m_doc and m_methods of the PyModuleDef at def."] [483 24 "// queue 270b: PyModule_GetDef"] [485 46 "// md_state (queue 269: PyModule_GetState), zeroed"] [498 1 "// ---- PyArg_Parse, PyArg_ParseTuple (Python/getargs.c) ----"] [500 1 "// vgetargs is vgetargs1_impl: the arguments (one, compat, for PyArg_Parse) converted by format into the pointers."] [591 1 "// seterror is getargs.c's seterror: a conversion's message as \"fname() argument N must be ...\"."] [615 1 "// argState is the va_list of the pointers the units store through."] [619 21 "// converttuple's item numbers of the failing unit (queue 270)"] [620 21 "// the Py_buffers filled, released on failure (freelist)"] [621 21 "// the pointers to the encoded strings' blocks, freed on failure"] [622 21 "// the O& converters that returned Py_CLEANUP_SUPPORTED and their addresses (queue 270b)"] [625 1 "// convert is convertitem (queue 270: the parenthesized tuples, capi_getargs.go): a failure's message or error, the"] [626 1 "// buffers and blocks the call filled given back on failure as cleanreturn's freelist."] [643 1 "// convertBuffer is convertbuffer: a bytes' contents, else the message of an object whose buffer is not read-only"] [644 1 "// (its type has bf_releasebuffer: bytearray, memoryview, array ...) (nil and no message: it has none, getbuffer's TypeError; queue 270)."] [657 1 "// noBuffer is PyObject_GetBuffer's TypeError for an object with no buffer (getbuffer's pending exception)."] [662 1 "// converterr is getargs.c's converterr."] [674 1 "// convert is convertsimple's units (b B h H i I n l k L K f d p y y# s s# z z# O O! and the tuple units aside):"] [675 1 "// a message (the conversion's failure) or an error (an exception the conversion raised)."] [841 12 "// a bytes or bytearray of length 1 as a char (getargs.c's convertsimple, queue 269)"] [856 12 "// a str of length 1 as an int (its code point)"] [873 1 "// ---- Py_BuildValue (Python/modsupport.c) ----"] [875 1 "// buildValue is Py_BuildValue's do_mkvalue over the format's units and the variadic arguments."] [993 2 "// the top level: one unit is its value, none is None, several a tuple"] [1015 1 "// ---- capsules (Objects/capsule.c) ----"] [1017 1 "// cCapsule is a capsule C made: its pointer, name (0: NULL), context and destructor in the world."] [1044 1 "// newCapsule is PyCapsule_New: a capsule of py's PyCapsule type, its destructor called on the library's next call"] [1045 1 "// after the capsule is collected."] [1060 5 "// the destructor gets the capsule (a fresh handle: the capsule is Go's until the call ends)"] [1071 1 "// capsuleImport is PyCapsule_Import."] [1105 1 "// decodeReplace is PyUnicode_FromFormat's %s: UTF-8 decoded with \"replace\"."] [1114 1 "// ---- slices (Objects/sliceobject.c) ----"] [1118 1 "// evalSliceIndex is _PyEval_SliceIndex: None leaves *v, an index clamps to Py_ssize_t."] [1144 1 "// sliceUnpack is PySlice_Unpack."] [1179 1 "// sliceAdjust is PySlice_AdjustIndices."] [1223 1 "// sliceGetIndices is PySlice_GetIndices: -1 without an exception for what it refuses."] [1276 1 "// ---- the frames (Python/ceval.c) ----"] [1278 1 "// callerFrame is the Python frame that called C (sys._getframe(0) seen from the native)."] [1299 1 "// frameLocals is PyEval_GetFrameLocals: a function's locals as a dict snapshot (PEP 667), a module's or class's"] [1300 1 "// namespace itself."] [1312 1 "// funcName and funcDesc are PyEval_GetFuncName and PyEval_GetFuncDesc."] [1348 1 "// sysCall calls sys.NAME(args...)."] [1361 1 "// sysGetObject is PySys_GetObject: sys's attribute (nil when absent; a decoding error is unraisable)."] [1380 1 "// ---- the natives ----"] [1382 1 "// version strings (Python/getversion.c, getplatform.c, getcopyright.c, getcompiler.c, Modules/getbuildinfo.c)"] [1398 2 "// version and build"] [1403 2 "// _Py_GetBuiltWithAssert (Python/getversion.c's): pyi's own runtime asserts nothing in C"] [1412 2 "// modules"] [1494 2 "// argument parsing and building"] [1519 2 "// errors (Python/errors.c)"] [1619 2 "// capsules"] [1653 2 "// the evaluation's state"] [1683 2 "// frames (Objects/frameobject.c: PyFrame_GetLocals and the others, new references)"] [1719 2 "// the GIL (Python/pystate.c): pyi's threads hold it when they run Python, so a thread that calls C holds it"] [1720 2 "// already: PyGILState_Ensure gives PyGILState_LOCKED (0) and Release has nothing to give back"] [1724 2 "// sys (Python/sysmodule.c)"] [1764 2 "// slices"] [1836 2 "// strings compared (Python/pystrcmp.c)"] [1869 1 "// cstr8 is a C string argument's bytes (nil for NULL)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[35 19] [36 31] [54 30] [82 27] [83 29] [112 28] [134 27] [147 43] [148 25] [182 18] [182 27] [201 27] [297 25] [312 16] [312 25] [323 30] [362 29] [460 19] [484 38] [487 30] [490 29] [491 34] [506 12] [506 24] [553 46] [579 12] [579 19] [646 26] [650 46] [680 48] [728 48] [799 26] [858 26] [928 14] [928 32] [929 42] [1124 45] [1149 41] [1164 49] [1173 47] [1226 26] [1306 23] [1315 46] [1321 46] [1322 24] [1327 26] [1335 46] [1342 26] [1388 39] [1389 23] [1417 55] [1440 60] [1454 60] [1461 62] [1497 23] [1500 53] [1512 58] [1530 28] [1557 103] [1563 29] [1565 31] [1566 28] [1605 24] [1614 20] [1678 74] [1741 23] [1758 24] [1767 24] [1850 13] [1850 103]]} (go/file "capi_limited.go" :imports [

